## DESCRIPTION
## Solve a 3 by 3 linear system that has a single solution.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by jjh2b

## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Systems of linear equations)
## DBsection(Systems with 3 variables)
## Date(September 5, 2008)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('lines')

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',             'PGML.pl',
    'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl', 'contextFraction.pl',
    'MatrixReduce.pl',           'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context('Vector');
Context()->noreduce('(-x)+y', '(-x)-y');

# Find a matrix with non-zero determinant and no zero row or column
$zerov = Vector(0, 0, 0);
do {
    $A = Matrix([
        [ random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5) ],
        [ random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5) ],
        [ random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5) ],
    ]);
    } until abs($A->det) > 0
    && abs($A->det) <= 4;

$x = Vector(random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4), random(-4, 4));
$b = $A * $x;

@lines = map {
    Formula($A->element($_, 1) . 'x+'
            . $A->element($_, 2) . 'y+'
            . $A->element($_, 3)
            . 'z')->reduce
} (1 .. 3);

Context('Point');
$xpt = Point($x);

$rma = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ['There is no solution to the linear system'],
        ['There are an infinite number of solutions to the linear system.'],
        [
            'There is a single solution to the linear system in the form %s',
            $xpt
        ]
    ],
    2
);

BEGIN_PGML
Solve the follow linear system using the Gauss-Jordon method: 

[``` \begin{aligned} 
[$lines[0]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(1) @] \\
[$lines[1]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(2) @] \\
[$lines[2]] & = [@ Matrix($b)->element(3) @] 
\end{aligned} ```]

[_]{$rma}

If the answer is a single point, write the point like "(1,2,3)"

END_PGML
Context('Fraction');    # for fraction arithmetic

# augmented matrix to be reduced
$aug = Matrix([
    [
        $A->element(1, 1),
        $A->element(1, 2),
        $A->element(1, 3),
        Matrix($b)->element(1)
    ],
    [
        $A->element(2, 1),
        $A->element(2, 2),
        $A->element(2, 3),
        Matrix($b)->element(2)
    ],
    [
        $A->element(3, 1),
        $A->element(3, 2),
        $A->element(3, 3),
        Matrix($b)->element(3)
    ]
]);

$aug_red = rref($aug);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

First, start with the augmented coefficient matrix or
[``` [$aug] ```]

and then perform Gauss-Jordon reduction to get 
[``` [$aug_red] ```]

Since the left 3 by 3 matrix is the identity matrix, the fourth column is the solution.
Written as a point the answer is [` [$xpt] `].
END_PGML_SOLUTION
COMMENT('The solution to this homogeneous system is a single point.');
ENDDOCUMENT();
